 "edit_add": {
  "spec": "The design open in SolidCraft is a shelving rack: four 20 x 20 mm posts P1..P4 at the corners of a 300 x 200 mm footprint, and four 10 mm shelves Shelf1..Shelf4 (with corner notches for the posts) at z = 50, 150, 250, 350. A circuit board named Board sits on fifteen standoffs S1..S15 that stand on Shelf1. Each is its own part. Change it: make the four posts 450 mm tall instead of 400 (still starting at z=0), and add a fifth shelf named Shelf5, the same as the other shelves (including the corner notches), with its bottom face at z=430. Change nothing else.",
  "setup": "for i,(x,y) in enumerate([(0,0),(280,0),(0,180),(280,180)]):\n    with part(f'P{i+1}'): box(20,20,400,at=(x,y,0),name=f'P{i+1}')\nfor i,z in enumerate((50,150,250,350)):\n    with part(f'Shelf{i+1}'):\n        box(300,200,10,at=(0,0,z),name=f'Shelf{i+1}')\n        for x,y in [(0,0),(280,0),(0,180),(280,180)]: box(20,20,10,at=(x,y,z),op='cut')\nwith part('Board'):\n    box(100,80,1.6,at=(100,60,70),name='Board')\n    for y in (70,100,130):\n        for x in (110,130,150,170,190): hole(at=(x,y,71.6),d=3.2)\ni=0\nfor y in (70,100,130):\n    for x in (110,130,150,170,190):\n        i+=1\n        with part(f'S{i}'):\n            cylinder(10,d=6,at=(x,y,60),name=f'S{i}')\n            hole(at=(x,y,70),d=3)",
